reims-vgpu: shader-evaluated blending on XR formats 551, 552, 553 and 555.

Metal: blending is available on every XR format. The AGX software blend
clamps the fragment's linear source to the format's published range before
the binary16 blend steps: the recovered PBE15 payload of 550/554,
0xbf40c0be..0x3fa0201d, is the documented decimal range -0.752941..1.25098
(the decoded codes 0 and 1022, rounded), not the exact code endpoints.
Before: `source_clamp` admitted only 550 and 554; a blended draw on 551, 552,
553 or 555 was refused with `vk_xr_blend_format_unqualified`.
Now: the clamp follows the rule the recovered payload follows. The sRGB
spellings 551, 553 and 555 clamp the linear source to their own published
range -0.5271..1.66894 (their decoded codes 0 and 1022, as the xr_upload
tables already cite from Apple's prose); 552 shares 554's colour range; every
XR alpha clamps to 0..1. Arithmetic, destination read and RTNE encoding are
unchanged. The refusal variant is removed; blend-colour and dual-source
factors keep `vk_xr_blend_factor_unsupported`.
Tests: `color_quantization::tests::source_over_on_every_xr_format_moves_into_the_shader_and_reads_its_target`,
`the_srgb_spellings_clamp_to_their_own_published_range_in_linear_light`
(unit); `vk_engine_parity::framebuffer_fetch_blends_every_remaining_xr_format_with_its_published_clamp`
on RADV (refused before): source-over twice over a clear stores codes
873/868/923 on the sRGB formats and 847/836/962 on 552; an opaque linear 2.0
stores 1022 (1023 unclamped) and 1.5 beside it stores 993 on an sRGB target
(947 with the linear formats' clamp bits).

